\begin{tikzpicture}[x=4mm,y=4mm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (8,0);
\coordinate (C) at (10.4,1.8); \coordinate (D) at (2.4,1.8);
\coordinate (E) at (0,5); \coordinate (F) at (8,5);
\coordinate (G) at (10.4,6.8); \coordinate (H) at (2.4,6.8);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(G)--(H)--(E)--cycle;
\draw (E)--(F)--(G) (B)--(F);
\draw[dashed] (A)--(D)--(C) (D)--(H);
\definecolor{diagonalred}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[diagonalred,thick] (A)--(G);
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,below right] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\path (A)--(E) node[midway,left] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\path (A) node[below left] {$A$} (B) node[below right] {$B$} (C) node[right] {$C$} (G) node[above right] {$G$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The longest rod follows the space diagonal $AG$. Use right-angled triangles $ABC$ and $ACG$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (4,0); \coordinate (C) at (4,3);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (3.7,0)--(3.7,0.3)--(4,0.3);
\path (A) node[below left] {$A$} (B) node[below right] {$B$} (C) node[above right] {$C$};
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,above left] {$AC$};
\begin{scope}[xshift=38mm]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0); \coordinate (Q) at (5,0); \coordinate (R) at (5,2.5);
\draw (P)--(Q)--(R)--cycle;
\draw (4.7,0)--(4.7,0.3)--(5,0.3);
\path (P) node[below left] {$A$} (Q) node[below right] {$C$} (R) node[above right] {$G$};
\path (P)--(Q) node[midway,below] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\path (Q)--(R) node[midway,right] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\path (P)--(R) node[midway,above left] {$AG$};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the base face diagonal and keep it exact.

$\begin{aligned}AC^{2}&=8^{2}+6^{2}\\AC^{2}&=100\\AC&=10\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$

Use the base diagonal and the vertical edge to find the space diagonal.

$\begin{aligned}AG^{2}&=AC^{2}+CG^{2}\\AG^{2}&=10^{2}+5^{2}\\AG^{2}&=125\\AG&=\sqrt{125}\text{ cm}\\AG&\approx11.18\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$

