examples.solution_text:
Let each edge have length $a\text{ cm}$. First use the base triangle, then the triangle containing the space diagonal.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (3,0); \coordinate (C) at (3,3);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (2.7,0)--(2.7,0.3)--(3,0.3);
\path (A) node[below left] {$A$} (B) node[below right] {$B$} (C) node[above right] {$C$};
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$a$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$a$};
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,above left] {$AC$};
\begin{scope}[xshift=34mm]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0); \coordinate (Q) at (4.24,0); \coordinate (R) at (4.24,3);
\draw (P)--(Q)--(R)--cycle;
\draw (3.94,0)--(3.94,0.3)--(4.24,0.3);
\path (P) node[below left] {$A$} (Q) node[below right] {$C$} (R) node[above right] {$G$};
\path (P)--(Q) node[midway,below] {$AC$};
\path (Q)--(R) node[midway,right] {$a$};
\path (P)--(R) node[midway,above left] {$18\text{ cm}$};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\begin{aligned}AC^{2}&=a^{2}+a^{2}\\AC^{2}&=2a^{2}\end{aligned}$

$\begin{aligned}AG^{2}&=AC^{2}+CG^{2}\\18^{2}&=2a^{2}+a^{2}\\324&=3a^{2}\\a^{2}&=108\\a&=\sqrt{108}\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$

Keep the edge length exact when calculating the volume.

$\begin{aligned}V&=a^{3}\\V&=(\sqrt{108})^{3}\\V&=108\sqrt{108}\\V&\approx1122.4\text{ cm}^{3}\end{aligned}$

$\begin{aligned}S&=6a^{2}\\S&=6\times108\\S&=648\text{ cm}^{2}\end{aligned}$
